{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"jq -r '.claims|to_entries[]|\\\"\\\\(.key): \\\\(.value.claim) [\\\\(.value.source_ids|join(\\\", \\\"))]\\\"' claims_grounding.json\"","aggregated_output":"0: Final qualification independently reports completed/qualified/true. This concerns documented integrity, coverage, execution and controls, not deployment validity. [final.qualification.status, final.qualification.outcome, final.qualification.correct]\n1: Aggregate final normalized reference agreement is 0.9975639445869278, rounded to 0.99756 in the abstract. [final.metric.reference_fidelity]\n2: All final structure-aware reference top-three overlaps and repeat-pair top-three/sign agreements equal one; these are separate assessments. [final.metric.top3_overlap, final.evidence.episodes]\n3: Stored vectors have zero maximum coordinate range across repeats within each fixed cap/model/query. [final.evidence.episodes]\n4: Pure reference sign agreement is 0.9994791667, not the mixed evaluator sign metric. [final.evidence.episodes, final.metric.signed_agreement]\n5: Mean normalized endpoint residual is 1.27919753412707e-11, control pass rate one, failed-call fraction zero and replay error zero. [final.metric.efficiency_error, final.metric.control_pass_rate, final.metric.failed_fraction, final.metric.replay_error]\n6: The recorded full workload takes 700.3707705293782 wall seconds, rounded to 700.37, including references, comparators, training and overhead; candidate-only latency is unavailable. [final.metric.wall_seconds]\n7: Four final dataset/model conditions are German logistic, German forest, ACS logistic and ACS forest; no additional task list or downstream study is present. [final.evidence.episodes]\n8: Final seeds are 104729, 130363 and 155921; caps 64/256/1024; six repeats per cap; sixteen fixed queries and training-background rows per fitted condition. [final.evidence.episodes]\n9: Final German retained splits are 300/100/100 records and twenty groups; ACS 20000/6667/6667 and ten groups. These are protocol counts, not independent explained-sample counts. [final.evidence.episodes]\n10: German uses original class code 2. ACS uses 2024 PUMS, native RELSHIPP without a RELP crosswalk, the retained adult filter and PINCP>50000 target. [final.evidence.episodes]\n11: German development/final content groups are disjoint. ACS uses California development and New York final data after excluding raw predictor-content overlaps. [final.evidence.episodes]\n12: Training-fitted ordinal vocabularies use unseen code -1; numeric medians and standardization are training fitted; queries/background use fixed ordering. [final.evidence.episodes]\n13: Logistic regression uses lbfgs, max_iter 500 and tolerance 1e-7. Forests use sixty-four trees, depth six and n_jobs one. [final.evidence.episodes]\n14: ACS references enumerate ten-feature finite games; German references average two independent cap-4096 library estimates. Their half-difference is a proxy, not a calibrated interval. [final.evidence.episodes]\n15: Stored 95-percent intervals use 1000 bootstrap resamples of sixteen query-level means after cap/repeat averaging, conditional on one fitted model/reference. [final.evidence.episodes]\n16: The normalized L1 agreement floor is 0.001; signs at magnitude at most 1e-8 are zero; top-three ties follow coordinate order. Endpoint residual is capped at one. [final.evidence.episodes]\n17: Library KernelExplainer uses identity link, l1_reg zero and nsamples equal to cap. Two independent split-cap calls each use floor(cap/2). [final.evidence.episodes]\n18: Forest attribution uses signed leaf-game beta-integral coefficients over all trees/background rows, intersecting repeated splits and retaining float32 predictor-input semantics. [final.evidence.episodes]\n19: Probability-scale logistic integration uses ceil(d/2) inclusion nodes, eight-node frequency panels, cutoff eight and at most 2048 frequency nodes; tail tolerance 1e-10 and mesh/efficiency tolerances 1e-8. [final.evidence.episodes]\n20: Two consecutive mesh agreements are required. Failure for any background row rejects integration; frequency-tail control is not a rigorous discretization bound. [final.evidence.episodes]\n21: Dispatch uses forest structure directly, then generic enumeration when cap covers 2^d-2 nontrivial coalitions before logistic integration; branch counts are unrecorded. [final.evidence.episodes]\n22: The sampled fallback combines independent complete paths and importance-corrected constrained regression. Alpha 0.05 separation is used only with at least two paths; acceptance coverage is absent. [final.evidence.episodes]\n23: The release contains independent validation routines without retained executions. They are not additional empirical controls. [final.evidence.episodes]\n24: Recorded dependencies include NumPy 2.1.3, SciPy 1.15.3, scikit-learn 1.6.1, SHAP 0.48.0, pandas 2.2.3 and folktables 0.0.12; a fresh full-lock installation was not tested. [final.evidence.episodes]\n25: German reference mean absolute coordinate half-differences are about 1.05e-4 logistic and 1.20e-4 forest; no error decomposition follows. [final.evidence.episodes]\n26: Seed-104729 query-bootstrap intervals round to [0.99618,0.99709] German logistic and [0.99292,0.99442] German forest. [final.evidence.episodes]\n27: Final cap-64 structure agreement is 0.9966/0.9937 German logistic/forest, versus library 0.9347/0.8806; ACS structure rounds to one versus library 0.9577/0.9636. [final.evidence.episodes]\n28: At cap 1024 final library means are 0.9889/0.9802 German logistic/forest and round to one for both ACS cases. This does not establish necessity of structure-aware access. [final.evidence.episodes]\n29: Split-cap German means at cap 64 are 0.3341/0.2995, recovering to 0.9699/0.9448 at cap 256; recorded diagnostics do not isolate a cause. [final.evidence.episodes]\n30: Final validation accuracy is 0.67 German logistic, 0.65--0.69 German forest, about 0.7609 ACS logistic and 0.7755--0.7773 ACS forest. Converged logistic fits use 19 and 13 iterations respectively. [final.evidence.episodes]\n31: Development uses seeds 1729/2718, eight queries, four repeated calls, caps 64/256; comparisons are supporting evidence, not held-out confirmation. [result.top_program_01, result.top_program_02, result.top_program_03]\n32: German cap-64 forest agreement changes from 0.858--0.870 to 0.9924--0.9929 with leaf computation; logistic from 0.946--0.951 to about 0.9963 with integration. [result.top_program_01, result.top_program_02, result.top_program_03]\n33: Custom sampled development means are nonmonotone from cap 64 to 256: ACS forest about 0.9674 to 0.9512 and German logistic 0.9488 to 0.9137; no unique cause is established. [result.top_program_01, result.top_program_02, result.top_program_03]\n34: Final table seed 104729, german_logistic, cap 64: agreement library 0.9292158063, split cap 0.3134347097, structure 0.9966775905; structure reference signs 1.0000000000, repeat metrics [1.0, 1.0], stored conditional query CI [0.9961794823135145, 0.9970868158424889]. [final.evidence.episodes]\n35: Final table seed 104729, german_logistic, cap 256: agreement library 0.9753728874, split cap 0.9713265507, structure 0.9966775905; structure reference signs 1.0000000000, repeat metrics [1.0, 1.0], stored conditional query CI [0.9961794823135145, 0.9970868158424889]. [final.evidence.episodes]\n36: Final table seed 104729, german_logistic, cap 1024: agreement library 0.9893991850, split cap 0.9892942724, structure 0.9966775905; structure reference signs 1.0000000000, repeat metrics [1.0, 1.0], stored conditional query CI [0.9961794823135145, 0.9970868158424889]. [final.evidence.episodes]\n37: Final table seed 104729, german_forest, cap 64: agreement library 0.8835736961, split cap 0.2903741391, structure 0.9936678394; structure reference signs 1.0000000000, repeat metrics [1.0, 1.0], stored conditional query 