{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat REPRODUCIBILITY.md; sed -n '1,43p' build_artifacts.py; cat source_evidence/evaluation/requirements.txt; jq '{count,queries,references:[.references[]|{citation_key,source_id,title,doi,url,evidence_path}]}' references_provenance.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat REPRODUCIBILITY.md; sed -n '1,43p' build_artifacts.py; cat source_evidence/evaluation/requirements.txt; jq '{count,queries,references:[.references[]|{citation_key,source_id,title,doi,url,evidence_path}]}' references_provenance.json\"","aggregated_output":"# Reproducing the fixed-game SHAP study\n\n## Measurement and source files\n\n`paper_data.json` is the immutable measurement registry. Final qualification is independently completed/qualified/true; this is an execution/integrity/control outcome, not deployment validity. Main results use final episodes separately from development selection. No downstream-study object or additional task list exists. No new training, explanations, independent validation routines, or evaluator execution occurred during writing.\n\n- `source_evidence/selected/`: retained structure-aware estimator, dispatch, response interface, specification and unexecuted independent validation routines.\n- `source_evidence/sampled/` and `source_evidence/forest/`: matched development implementation snapshots.\n- `source_evidence/evaluation/`: final/development evaluators, acquisition code, pinned requirements and data provenance.\n- `task/resources/{search,final}/`: frozen records accessible through the supplied task link.\n- `analysis_summary.json`: descriptive reductions of recorded observations, not additional experiments.\n- `claims_grounding.json`: registry claim mappings and readable implementation evidence locations.\n- `source_evidence/MANIFEST.json`: hashes of copied evidence, for provenance rather than substantive implementation support.\n\n## Environment and public data\n\nThe supplied scientific environment has Python 3.12.15. Recorded requirements include NumPy 2.1.3, SciPy 1.15.3, scikit-learn 1.6.1, SHAP 0.48.0, pandas 2.2.3 and folktables 0.0.12. Their installed metadata was inspected. The complete pinned requirements are preserved, but a fresh installation was not tested:\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -m venv /tmp/shap-study-env\n/tmp/shap-study-env/bin/pip install -r source_evidence/evaluation/requirements.txt\n```\n\nThe evaluator requires Linux isolation, CPU affinity and Landlock/seccomp. A non-Linux port was not tested. BLAS thread limits are set in the evaluator; forest fitting uses one thread.\n\nExact acquisition URLs, digests, licensing, release metadata and normalization are in `source_evidence/evaluation/data_provenance.json`. German is UCI Statlog German Credit, DOI 10.24432/C5NC77, under CC BY 4.0. ACS uses actual 2024 one-year CA and NY PUMS releases, with native `RELSHIPP` replacing absent historical `RELP`, without an invented crosswalk. This is not unmodified historical ACSIncome. All cross-state predictor-content overlaps are removed before ACS selection; one representative per content group is retained with duplicate/conflicting-label provenance.\n\nUse the frozen resources for offline reproduction. To recapture independently, download every `sources[*].url` to `/tmp/public-source/<sources[*].file>`, verify the recorded SHA256, then run:\n\n```sh\npython source_evidence/evaluation/capture.py \\\n  --source_dir /tmp/public-source --output_root /tmp/new-resources\n```\n\nNo recapture was performed during writing. The frozen resources suffice for evaluation if upstream archives change.\n\n## Evaluation command (documented, not rerun)\n\n```sh\nTASK_SOURCE_DIR=\"$PWD/task\" /tmp/shap-study-env/bin/python \\\n  source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py \\\n  --program_path \"$PWD/source_evidence/selected/program.py\" \\\n  --results_dir /tmp/shap-final-reproduction\n```\n\nFinal seeds: 104729, 130363, 155921; caps: 64, 256, 1024; six calls per cap, sixteen fixed queries and background rows per condition. Development seeds: 1729, 2718; caps: 64, 256; eight queries and four calls. The full recorded final wall total is 700.3707705293782 seconds, including references, comparators, training and overhead. It is not guaranteed runtime, CPU-hours or candidate-only latency. No equal-time comparison is available.\n\n## Figures and tables\n\nRendering tools live in a private environment outside this manuscript workspace:\n\n```sh\npython -m venv /tmp/paper-tools\n/tmp/paper-tools/bin/pip install numpy matplotlib pillow jsonschema pypdf requests Unidecode\n/tmp/paper-tools/bin/python build_artifacts.py\n```\n\n- `final_reference_comparison`: final non-replay cells and baseline metrics by dataset/model/cap.\n- `component_comparison`: matched development cells for forest and logistic components, never relabeled as held-out evidence.\n- `reference_diagnostics`: final German candidate/reference distances and recorded reference half-differences, not error bounds.\n- All numerical tables: generated by `build_artifacts.py` under `tables/`. The manuscript embeds those rows directly to keep the supplementary section self-contained. Regeneration updates fragments, not the manuscript; a change of measurements requires an audited manuscript revision.\n- `fixed_game_overview`: orchestrator-owned conceptual render. The guarded placeholder and empty plan stub are replaced synchronously after this step. Reusable code cannot overwrite the completed render. It contains no measured-result placeholder.\n\nQuantitative plots export vector PDF and 300-DPI PNG; LaTeX uses PDFs. Full text width is 5.5 inches and plotted labels are at least nine points. Sidecars connect generated artifacts to recorded inputs. The paper reports pure reference sign agreement rather than misinterpreting the evaluator's mixed reference/repeat sign summary.\n\n## Manuscript and literature\n\nThe official ICLR 2026 archive was retrieved from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ICLR/Master-Template/master/iclr2026.zip`. Original style files are in `template_evidence/`, with copies at `paper.sty` and `paper.bst`; anonymous review mode is retained. `VENUE.md` fixes 2026 as the target year even though the repository contains other years.\n\n`curate_references.py` retrieves known permitted primary works by DOI or exact title through OpenAlex. Semantic Scholar was rate-limited. Primary records and available abstracts were read; citing/reference graphs and related pages were not traversed. `literature_evidence/` preserves the selected records. An incorrect initial Owen DOI returned unrelated tuberculosis metadata; it was rejected immediately, never cited, and corrected to *Multilinear Extensions of Games*. No prohibited study was identified or deliberately sought. Earlier retrieval noise was discarded rather than described as read literature. This does not retroactively certify every earlier-stage retrieval as reviewed.\n\n```sh\npdflatex -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex\nbibtex paper\npdflatex -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex\npdflatex -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex\n```\n\n`writing_validation.json` distinguishes completed checks, environmental validator limitations and the pending diagram. The scientific-evidence report must contain zero dangling references. LLM roles are disclosed in the manuscript. Query-bootstrap intervals do not cover reference bias, retraining or background uncertainty. Structural access and small fixed query sets prevent deployment, causal, human or new-population claims.\nimport ast\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use('Agg')\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport numpy as np\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw\n\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nCOLORS = {'standard': '#c17b14', 'multistart': '#956ba5', 'structure': '#176b8c'}\nCASE_NAMES = {'german_logistic': 'German / logistic', 'german_forest': 'German / forest', 'acs_logistic': 'ACS / logistic', 'acs_forest': 'ACS / forest'}\nplt.rcParams.update({'font.size': 10, 'axes.labelsize': 10, 'axes.titlesize':